model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The dashboard's built server render highlights code with an engine that carries only the TypeScript, JSON and shell grammars, so the other grammars stay out of the dashboard Worker's upload. Code in those three languages is colored in the server's HTML, and hydration keeps those colors because each line holds the same text and the browser's engine yields the same tokens. Any other language renders plain on the server, where the engine fails it as unavailable instead of throwing, and takes its colors once the browser's full engine loads. A dev server renders with the full engine. The server build fails if it no longer swaps the engine; production upload checks require the three grammars in the dashboard upload, reject every other grammar and the full engine there, refuse a chunk they cannot read, and require the browser build's own highlight engine chunk. Worker upload and startup budgets stay unchanged."
    }
  }
}
